  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Given that $P(x)=x^3+bx^2+cx+d$ has roots $p,q,r$, determine a monic polynomial with roots $2p,2q$, and $2r$, expressing its coefficients in terms of $b,c$, and $d$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$Q(x)=x^3+2bx^2+4cx+8d$.\n\nUse $Q(x)=8P\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)$ to double the roots and retain a leading coefficient of $1$.",
      "worked": "Since $P$ is monic with roots $p,q,r$,\n$$P(x)=(x-p)(x-q)(x-r).$$\n$$\\begin{align*}P\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)&=\\left(\\frac{x}{2}-p\\right)\\left(\\frac{x}{2}-q\\right)\\left(\\frac{x}{2}-r\\right)\\\\P\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)&=\\frac18(x-2p)(x-2q)(x-2r).\n\\end{align*}$$\nThus $8P\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)$ is monic and has the required roots.\n$$\\begin{align*}Q(x)&=8P\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)\\\\Q(x)&=8\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)^3+8b\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)^2+8c\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+8d\\\\Q(x)&=x^3+2bx^2+4cx+8d.\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 62
  },
